  "name": "Brasil FurFest",
  "shortName": "BFF",
  "description": "Brasil FurFest (BFF) is an annual furry convention in Brazil, created in 2016 by members of the Brazilian fandom and launched through a crowdfunding campaign. The first edition, held September 9 to 11, 2016, at the Mercure Santos Hotel in Santos, São Paulo, drew 169 attendees. The convention stayed in Santos through 2024, held online events in 2020 and 2021, and then moved to São Paulo city in 2025 and Campinas in 2026, when it had 1,512 attendees. Each edition raises money for animal welfare projects, mainly SOS Vida Pet Litoral. The 2027 edition moves to CENACON in Poços de Caldas, Minas Gerais. Since 2026 it has been organized by BFF Eventos e Intermediação LTDA.",
